This namelist performs a pancake collapse simulation with dark matter only.
You need a ascii file for the initial conditions. You can execute the script
python3 ./utils/py/pancake.py
This will generate a file named ic_part in the parent folder.
To compile the code with MPI (recommended), type in folder /bin the command line:
make NDIM=1 MPI=1 UNITS=COSMO GRAV=1 HYDRO=0
Then execute the code in the parent folder using:
mpirun -np 2 bin/ramses1d namelist/pancake.nml

&RUN_PARAMS
cosmo=.true.
pic=.true.
poisson=.true.
hydro=.false.
nrestart=0
nsubcycle=1,1,2
ncontrol=1
verbose=.false.
/

&OUTPUT_PARAMS
delta_aout=0.1
aend=1.0
/

&INIT_PARAMS
filetype='ascii'
initfile(1)='.'
H0=72.
omega_m=0.3
omega_l=1.0
boxlen_ini=25.
aexp_ini=0.01
/

&AMR_PARAMS
levelmin=10
levelmax=10
ngridmax=20000
npartmax=40000
nexpand=1,
/

&POISSON_PARAMS
epsilon=1.d-4
/

&REFINE_PARAMS
m_refine=10*8.,
/
